  "topic_en": "Identities between theta-type series (1 − 2x + 2x^4 − …, 1 + 2x + 2x^4 + …) and their variants in x^3, derived by subtraction and multiplication of earlier numbered formulas and expressed as infinite products in the bracket notation [x^n].",
  "transcription": "Aus der Subtraction von 38 u. 30\n[37] $\\{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}\\}-(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-\\}=2(1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{3}{8}}}\\left(x^{\\frac{25}{8}}+x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{289}{8}}+x^{\\frac{361}{8}}+\\&c.\\right)$\nSetzt man in 6 statt $x$, $x^6$ u. statt $y$, $x^5y$ so wird\n$(1+x^{11}y)(1+x^{23}y)(1+x^{35}y)\\cdots(1+\\frac{x}{y})(1+\\frac{x^{13}}{y})(1+\\frac{x^{25}}{y})\\cdots[x^{12}]=1+\\frac{x}{y}+x^{11}y+\\frac{x^{14}}{yy}+x^{34}yy+\\&c.$\nAlso die Zerlegung in Factoren\n[38] $\\{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}+\\}-\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-\\}=2x^3[x^{36}](1+x^3)(1+x^{33})(1+x^{39})(1+x^{69})\\cdots(1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\cdots$\n[39] $\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}\\cdots\\}-\\{1-2x+2x^4-\\}=2x[x^{12}](1+x)(1+x^{11})(1+x^{13})(1+x^{23})\\cdots(1-x)(1-x^3)(1-x^5)\\cdots$\n[40] $\\{1+2x^3+2x^{12}+2x^{27}\\}-\\{1+2x^9+2x^{36}+\\}=2x^3[x^{36}](1-x^3)(1-x^{33})(1-x^{39})(1-x^{69})\\cdots(1+x^3)(1+x^9)(1+x^{15})\\cdots$\n[41] $\\{1+2x+2x^4+2x^9\\}-\\{1+2x^3+2x^{12}+\\}=2x[x^{12}](1-x)(1-x^{11})(1-x^{13})(1-x^{23})\\cdots(1+x)(1+x^3)(1+x^5)\\cdots$\nAus der Subtraction von 29 u. 30 folgt\n[42] $\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}\\}-\\{1-2x+2x^4-\\}=2(1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\cdots\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{9}{8}}-x^{\\frac{25}{8}}-x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{81}{8}}+x^{\\frac{225}{8}}-\\&c\\right\\}$\nWoraus die Zerlegung des letzten Gliedes dieser Gleichung in Factoren folgt\nAus der Multiplication von 38 u. 39 folgt\n[43] $\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}\\}^2-\\{1-2x+2x^4-\\}^2=4x[x^{12}]^2(1-x)^2(1-x^3)^2(1-x^5)^2\\cdots(1+x)(1+x^5)(1+x^7)(1+x^{11})\\cdots$\n$=4x\\frac{[x^{12}]^2[x]^2}{[xx]^2}\\cdot\\frac{[xx]^2\\;[x^3][x^{12}]}{[x][x^4]\\;[x^6]^2}=4x\\frac{[x][x^3][x^{12}]^3}{[x^4][x^6]^2}$\nEben so aus der Multiplication von 36 u. 41\n[44] $\\{1+2x^3+2x^{12}+2x^{27}\\}^2-\\{1+2x+2x^4+\\}^2=4x[x^{12}]^2(1+x)^2(1+x^3)^2(1+x^5)^2\\cdots(1-x)(1-x^5)(1-x^7)(1-x^{11})\\cdots$\n$=4x\\frac{[x^{12}]^2[xx]^4}{[x]^2[x^4]^2}\\,\\frac{[x]\\;[x^6]}{[xx]\\;[x^3]}=4x\\frac{[xx]^3[x^6][x^{12}]^2}{[x][x^3][x^4]^2}$\nAlso der Quotient\n[45] $\\frac{(1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27})^2-(1-2x+2x^4\\cdots)^2}{(1+2x^3+2x^{12}+2x^{27})^2-(1+2x+2x^4)^2}=-\\left(\\frac{1-x}{1+x}\\right)^3\\left(\\frac{1-x^3}{1+x^3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1-x^5}{1+x^5}\\right)^3\\left(\\frac{1-x^7}{1+x^7}\\right)^3\\left(\\frac{1-x^9}{1+x^9}\\right)\\cdots=-\\frac{[x]^2[x^3]^2[x^4][x^{12}]}{[xx]^3[x^6]^3}$\nund das Product\n[45b] $\\{(1-2x^3)^2-(1-2x)^2\\}\\{(1+2x^3)^2-(1+2x)^2\\}=-16xx\\frac{[xx]^3[x^{12}]^5}{[x^4]^3[x^6]}$",
